    "updated_at": "2017-08-02T11:59:41Z",
    "body": "I can't get there programmatically.\r\n```html\r\n<iframe src=/></iframe>\r\n<script>\r\nonload = () => {\r\n  self[0].location.hash = \"t1\"\r\n  w(self[0].location.hash)\r\n  self[0].location.hash = \"t2\"\r\n  w(self[0].location.hash)\r\n  self[0].location.hash = \"t3\"\r\n  w(self[0].location.hash)\r\n  history.back();\r\n  setTimeout(() => {\r\n    w(self[0].location.hash)\r\n    self[0].location.replace(\"/#something\");\r\n    setTimeout(() => {\r\n      w(self[0].location.hash)\r\n      history.forward();\r\n      setTimeout(() => {\r\n        w(self[0].location.hash);\r\n      }, 200);\r\n    }, 200);\r\n  }, 200);\r\n}\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\nIn [Live DOM Viewer](http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/) does something entirely different in Firefox compared to Chrome. Firefox basically doesn't navigate back or forward.\r\n\r\ncc @smaug---- ",
